<div>
    <p>Read-only admin viewer over <code>spatie/laravel-activitylog</code> (v5.1). "Create" is disabled and every field is read-only — nothing should hand-create or hand-edit a log row.</p>
    <p>To opt another model into logging, add <code>App\Nexus\Modules\ActivityLog\Traits\LogsActivityWithTranslatable</code> — it logs every dirty attribute change, skips empty (no-op) log entries, and automatically decodes Spatie-Translatable JSON columns (declared via <code>public $translatable</code>) so a translated field's diff reads as a normal array, not a raw JSON string. Already wired into <code>User</code>, <code>ShopProduct</code>, and <code>Promotion</code>. Override <code>getActivitylogOptions()</code> (call <code>$this->getDefaultLogOptions()</code> as a base) to customize which attributes are logged — see <code>User::getActivitylogOptions()</code>, which excludes <code>password</code>/<code>remember_token</code> from the base "log everything" default.</p>
    <p>The <code>causer</code> column on the view screen links to the acting admin user when the actor was authenticated, or shows "System / Deleted user" otherwise (a guest action, a queued job, or a since-deleted account).</p>
</div>
